## Known Limitations & Live Testing Notes

Each entry in `sod_policies` is populated by the same conversion code as
the singular [`identitynow_sod_policy_v1` data source](../data-sources/sod_policy_v1.md) -
see its "Known Limitations & Live Testing Notes" section for the full list
of limitations shared by both.

`GET /sod-policies/v1` supports server-side `filters` and `sorters` query
parameters (the standard [V3 API collection parameters](https://developer.sailpoint.com/idn/api/standard-collection-parameters)
syntax), unlike `identitynow_segments_v1`'s equivalent list endpoint. The
API's own `count` query parameter (an `X-Total-Count` header toggle) is
intentionally dropped from this schema entirely - `count` is a reserved
root attribute/block name in Terraform, matching
`identitynow_governance_groups_v1`/`identitynow_segments_v1`'s equivalent
precedent.

**Be aware this data source performs a live API call at `terraform plan`
time whenever its arguments are fully known** (i.e. not derived from
another resource's unknown output) - harmless in normal use, but means a
`main.tf` exercising this data source is not appropriate if you're trying
to keep a `plan` check fully credential-free.
